title: The Berlin Opposition
subtitle: A great district turns against the Zentrale.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 10 and offensive_gone = 0 and unionist_gone = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.leader();
Q.e22_opp = (Q.lead_code == 2) ? 'unionist' : 'offensive';
Q.e22_opp_a = Q.lead_code == 2 ? 'brandler' : 'fischer';
Q.e22_opp_b = Q.lead_code == 2 ? 'thalheimer' : 'maslow';
Q.e22_opp_free = (RG.isFree(Q.e22_opp_a) || RG.isFree(Q.e22_opp_b)) ? 1 : 0;
!}

= The Berlin Opposition

[? if lead_code != 2 : The Berlin district has become a party within the party. Ruth Fischer and Arkadi Maslow say the united front has turned into polite letters to the SPD executive. Their resolutions call the workers' government a social democratic swindle. Thälmann's Hamburg is starting to agree with them. ?][? if lead_code = 2 : With the Left in the Zentrale, the opposition comes from Saxony. Brandler and Thalheimer say the Fischer line is driving every union man out of the party, and they write to Moscow more often than to Berlin. ?]

The opposition has its own platform, its own meetings and its own friends on the Executive.

- @remove: Take their posts from them.
- @seats: Give them seats in the Zentrale.
- @moscow: Ask the Executive to arbitrate.

@remove
subtitle: The Zentrale's authority holds. The next congress will be bitter.
view-if: e22_opp_free = 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.setRole(Q.e22_opp_a, 'Removed from the district leadership');
RG.setRole(Q.e22_opp_b, 'Removed from the district leadership');
Q[Q.e22_opp + '_satisfaction'] -= 12;
Q.e22_berlin_opposition = 1;
RG.ecci(Q.e22_opp == 'offensive' ? 'zinoviev' : 'radek', -5);
!}

The Central Committee bans factional circulars and removes the opposition's leaders from their district posts. Their followers now meet in back rooms instead of the district office, and start counting delegates.

@seats
subtitle: The opposition becomes the junior partner, and its line weighs on ours.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_berlin_opposition = 2;
Q.junior_faction = Q.e22_opp;
Q[Q.e22_opp + '_satisfaction'] += 12;
Q['lean_' + Q.e22_opp] += 2;
Q.unity += 4;
!}

Two of the opposition take seats in the Zentrale. Its meetings get longer and louder.

@moscow
subtitle: Zinoviev decides. The quarrel goes quiet until he wants it loud again.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_berlin_opposition = 3;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 8);
Q.independence -= 6;
Q.unity += 3;
!}

Zinoviev and Radek summon both sides to Moscow, praise both, and recommend unity. The opposition comes home with a promise that the next congress will hear its theses.
